Subject: winegstreamer: no GL display on macOS

The display itself is harmless -- with GST_GL_WINDOW=x11 not compiled in, it
is an inert dummy -- but a non-NULL display flips wg_parser_create()'s
"use_opengl && gl_display" gate, and the glupload chain then creates a Cocoa
GL CONTEXT. gst_gl_invoke_on_main() hands that to the process's Cocoa main
thread; the block faults, and Wine's init_handler runs on a thread with no
Wine TEB, poisoning its TSD base before any handler logic. The main thread
freezes inside a mach trap where signals are never delivered: the main
dispatch queue stops draining, CFRunLoopWakeUp is a no-op, and every
OnMainThread() caller in winemac.drv deadlocks. Observed as a 32-bit
DirectShow RenderFile that never returns -- SSFIV frozen on its first movie --
while 64-bit passes by never requesting GL (wm_reader enables it only for
sizeof(void*) == 4).

The trade, stated plainly: 32-bit wm_reader loses the GL I420->RGBA converter
chain it requests for exactly this case, and colour-converts on the CPU
instead. That path never worked on macOS (the process froze before a single
frame), so nothing that works today is lost; if the foreign-thread fault
handling is ever hardened, this can be revisited.

tests/gstreamer/dshow-render-test.sh reproduces the hang in both bitnesses
without Steam or a game.

diff --git a/dlls/winegstreamer/unixlib.c b/dlls/winegstreamer/unixlib.c
index b259388026b..30fecd57ba5 100644
--- a/dlls/winegstreamer/unixlib.c
+++ b/dlls/winegstreamer/unixlib.c
@@ -323,8 +323,22 @@ NTSTATUS wg_init_gstreamer(void *arg)
     if (!gst_element_register_winegstreamerstepper(NULL))
         GST_ERROR("Failed to register the stepper element");
 
+    /* Not on macOS. The display itself is harmless (with GST_GL_WINDOW=x11
+     * unavailable it is an inert dummy), but a non-NULL display flips
+     * wg_parser_create()'s "use_opengl && gl_display" gate, and the glupload
+     * chain then creates a Cocoa GL CONTEXT -- whose gst_gl_invoke_on_main()
+     * block faults on the Cocoa main thread, where Wine's init_handler has no
+     * TEB and poisons the thread. The whole process's main thread freezes and
+     * every winemac.drv OnMainThread() caller deadlocks: a 32-bit DirectShow
+     * RenderFile that never returns (tests/gstreamer/dshow-render-test.sh).
+     * The trade: 32-bit wm_reader loses its GL I420->RGBA converter and falls
+     * back to videoconvert on the CPU. See docs/proton-migration.md, 0035. */
+#ifdef __APPLE__
+    GST_INFO("Not creating a GL display; the GL element chain deadlocks on macOS.");
+#else
     if (!(gl_display = gst_gl_display_new()))
         GST_ERROR("Failed to create OpenGL display");
+#endif
 
     if (!media_converter_init())
     {
